---
title: "Overlays"
---

Overlays are used for displaying messages over the top of the grid.
There are built-in overlays triggered by grid state and custom overlays triggered by the application.

## Grid Overlays

The grid provides the following built-in overlays that will be shown automatically based on grid state unless disabled:
- Loading overlay - shown when data is loading
- No rows overlay - shown when there are no rows to display
- No matching filter overlay - shown when no rows match the current filter
- Excel export overlay - shown when data is being exported to Excel

### Loading

{% metaTag tags=["showLoadingOverlay"] /%}

The loading overlay is displayed when the grid property `loading` is set to `true` and takes precedence over other provided overlays.

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="overlays" names=["loading"] /%}

 If the `loading` property is not provided, the grid automatically displays the loading overlay until both `rowData` and `columnDefs` are supplied with non-null values for the first time. This behaviour can be suppressed by setting `loading` to `false` before initialising the grid.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Loading overlay" name="loading-overlay"  exampleHeight=350 /%}

### No Rows

When `rowData` is set to an empty array `[]`, the grid automatically displays the no-rows overlay.

{% gridExampleRunner title="No Rows Overlay" name="no-rows-overlay"  exampleHeight=350 /%}

### No Matching Filter

When a filter is applied and no rows match the filter criteria, the grid automatically displays the no-matching-filter overlay.

{% gridExampleRunner title="No Matching Filter Overlay" name="no-matching-filter-overlay"  exampleHeight=350 /%}

### Excel Export

When exporting data to Excel, the grid automatically displays the excel-export overlay until the export is complete.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Excel Export Overlay" name="excel-export-overlay"  exampleHeight=350 /%}

## Suppress Grid Overlays
Each grid overlay can be suppressed via the `suppressOverlays` grid option. This option accepts an array of overlay types to suppress.

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="overlays" names=["suppressOverlays"] /%}

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    // suppress the no-rows overlay showing when there are no rows
    suppressOverlays: [ 'agNoRowsOverlay'],
};
```

## Custom Grid Overlays

There are different ways to customise the provided overlays depending on your requirements:

 - `overlayComponent` - provide a single custom overlay component for all overlay types
 - `overlayComponentSelector` - dynamically provide custom overlay components based on the overlay type
 - `components` map - provide custom overlay components by registering them in the components map


### Overlay Component

Provide a custom overlay component to the `overlayComponent` grid option. This component will be used in place of all the provided overlays and can be configured to display different content based on the `params.defaultOverlay` property.

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="overlays" names=["overlayComponent", "overlayComponentParams"] /%}

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    overlayComponent: CustomOverlay,
    overlayComponentParams: {
        myLoadingMessage: 'Custom loading message',
        myNoRowsMessage: 'Custom no rows message'
    },
};
```

### Overlay Component Selector

Dynamically provide different overlay components for each provided overlay type via the `overlayComponentSelector` grid option. The selector function is called with a parameter object containing the `defaultOverlay` property which indicates the type of overlay the grid is about to display. Custom parameters can also be supplied via the returned object's `params` property alongside with the custom `component`.

Returning `undefined` from the selector function will cause the grid to use the default overlay component for that overlay type.

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="overlays" names=["overlayComponentSelector"] /%}

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    overlayComponentSelector: (params) => {
        if (params.defaultOverlay === 'agLoadingOverlay') {
            return {
                component: CustomLoadingOverlay,
                params: {
                    loadingMessage: 'Please wait while data is loading...'
                }
            };
        }
        // return undefined to use the provided overlay for other overlay types
        return undefined;
    },
};
```

### Components Map

Each provided overlay can be replaced with a custom component by assigning a custom component to the provided overlay key in the [`components` map](./components). Custom parameters can be supplied via the `overlayComponentParams` grid option and these will be passed to all overlay components.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    components: {
        agLoadingOverlay: CustomLoadingOverlay,
        agNoRowsOverlay: CustomNoRowsOverlay
    },
    overlayComponentParams: {
        loadingMessage: 'Please wait while data is loading...',
        noRowsMessage: 'No data available'
    }
};
```

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="overlays" names=["components", "overlayComponentParams"] /%}

